Table \ref{tab:big models} shows the performance of The SGT for large models. Across all three models the SGT maintains utility to within 0.5pp of their respective baseline models. The SGT for Qwen3 had the highest utility (-0.29pp); however, its SymTTR-100 was lowest (66.39\%) as was its rank histogram entropy (67.67\%). This suggests that further hyperparameter tuning (e.g. increasing the strength of the \sgtmi \ loss) could further improve performance. The remaining metrics are all higher than what was observed in the Llama-1B loss ablation likely due to the substantially longer training time allocated to these models. Overall, the protection offered by the SGT for the large models is high in both transformation metrics and information theoretic measures.

