% To address the computational challenges posed by this complex system, we proposed a suite of energy-stable numerical schemes. Spatial discretization is achieved via the local discontinuous Galerkin (LDG) method, ensuring high-order accuracy and adaptability. We designed a first-order, decoupled temporal scheme and rigorously proved its unconditional energy stability. To enhance temporal accuracy, we further employed a semi-implicit spectral deferred correction (SDC) method, enabling high-order convergence in both time and space.

