\textbf{Guessing Anomaly:} Test-takers may answer based on luck or incomplete understanding of the question, which does not accurately reflect their true abilities. To assess the impact of anomalies on test results, Anomaly Management utilizes the cognitive diagnosis ability \(\theta\) to assist in judgment. For a question \(q\) where TestAgent receives feedback label \(y\), cognitive diagnosis estimate the probability \(P(q,y)\) of the test-taker answering question \(q\) with label \(y\) based on the current ability \(\theta\). If the current ability value makes it difficult to answer with label \(y\), Autonomous Feedback Mechanism is employed for judgment.

\textbf{Misleading Anomaly:} In the case of Misleading Anomaly, test-takers deliberately provide incorrect answers, possibly due to lack of interest in the test or psychological resistance to the question. Anomaly Management conducts reasoning based on context. By tracking the context of the test, inconsistencies or contradictions in a test-taker's responses to multiple questions on the same topic can be identified. For instance, if a test-taker provides a correct definition of a concept in one question but contradicts it in subsequent questions, it may be intentionally misleading. Anomaly Management then dissects the question to engage in more detailed dialogue to avoid such issues. 

\textbf{Overconfidence Anomaly:} 
Overconfidence Anomaly occurs when test-takers show excessive confidence in answers, even when uncertain. Anomaly Management accepts responses but requests reasons for answers. If high confidence lacks sufficient reasoning in explanations, the model deems it unfounded. Anomaly Management and Autonomous Feedback Mechanism complement each other. Successful detection often requires new questions to verify anomalies, enhancing test precision.
% 在具体测试时，测试者可能因为猜测恰好猜对了答案，也可能会故意回答一些错误的答案等。这些情况在实际情况中都有出现。为此我们将Anomaly具体分为三种，Guessing Anomaly ， Misleading Anomaly，Overconfidence Anomaly .对于Guessing Anomaly，测试者可能因为运气或者不完全理解问题而进行回答，这不能准确反映测试者的真实能力。对于Misleading Anomaly测试者故意给出错误的答案，可能出于各种原因，例如对测试不感兴趣、对问题存在抵触心理等。这种情况下很难检测。对于Overconfidence Anomaly测试者在回答问题时可能表现出过度的自信，甚至在自己不确定的情况下也给出肯定的回答。

% 尽管我们难以减少测试者自身的主观因素，我们可以尽可能避免这三种Anomaly从而增加测试的准确度。对于Guessing Anomaly ，Anomaly Management结合认知诊断来分析。为了异常对对测试结果的影响，Anomaly Management使用认知诊断的能力$\theta$予以辅助判定。对于题目$q$,TestAgent得到的反馈标签是$y$。认知诊断会根据当前的能力$\theta$，估计测试者答题$q$标签为$y$的概率$P(q,y)$\citep{xxx}。倘若判定当前能力值难以回答标签为$y$。则交给Autonomous Feedback Mechanism来判断。对于Misleading Anomaly，Anomaly Management结合上下文进行推理，通过追踪测试的上下文，可以识别测试者回答是否符合逻辑。如果同一主题的多个问题得出的答案不一致或相互矛盾，大模型可以标记此种异常。例如，测试者在前面回答了某个概念的正确定义，但在后续问题中给出与之冲突的回答，则有可能是故意误导。这种情况Anomaly Management会将问题拆解，以更细腻的对话咨询测试者回避的问题。对于Overconfidence Anomaly，Anomaly Management不仅仅接受测试者的回答，还要求对答案的理由或解释。如果测试者在回答时表现出高度自信，但在解释为什么选择某个答案时缺乏充分的理由或逻辑，则模型可以判定其自信是无依据的。

% Anomaly Management与Autonomous Feedback Mechanism相辅相成，互相结合。当异常判定成功时往往需要新一轮的问题来检定异常，增加测试的精度。

