\textit{Metrics}. We use Performance Ratio to measure the performance of all algorithms, defined as the ratio of the total utility obtained by an algorithm to the optimal utility for $\mathbf{P}$ (the optimal utility is obtained by solving $\mathbf{P}$ using the ILP solver Gurobi, with a timeout limit set to 10 minutes).
