\section{Conclusion}
In this paper, we address the novel challenge of uncertainty quantification in survival analysis and propose SurvUnc, a meta-model based framework that incorporates an anchor-based learning strategy. We establish systematic evaluation protocols to assess uncertainty quantification methods on survival models. Extensive experiments conducted across multiple datasets and survival models demonstrate the effectiveness and robustness of SurvUnc in uncertainty quantification. Furthermore, its model-agnostic design ensures compatibility with a wide range of survival models, offering valuable insights into uncertainty quantification for survival analysis. Future work will explore uncertainty quantification for survival analysis with competing events and time-varying covariates, as well as evaluate SurvUnc in the context of foundation model-based survival analysis \cite{jeanselme2024review,gu2025time}.


