The main contributions of this paper are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
    \item We propose a novel cluster stability detection method that identifies unstable clusters by analyzing dynamic changes in sample assignment during iteration. This replaces traditional complex computations and manual intervention.

    \item We design a strategy that jointly deletes unstable clusters and adjusts the vigilance parameter, enabling its self-adaptation and improving robustness without introducing additional predefined parameters.
\end{itemize}

