\section{Conclusion}

% 传统的FuzzyART算法对警戒参数ρ的敏感程度高，对先验知识提出了高要求。为解决这个问题，我们针对Fuzzy ART的重复迭代过程进行启发式改进，形成新的聚类算法Iterative Refinement Fuzzy Adaptive Resonance Theory (IR-ART)。IR-ART将三个关键阶段融合到迭代过程中，不断地删除不稳定类簇并微调警戒参数。
\noindent Fuzzy ART is highly sensitive to the vigilance parameter, which places significant demands on prior knowledge. To address this issue, we optimize the iterative process of Fuzzy ART and propose Iterative Refinement Fuzzy Adaptive Resonance Theory (IR-ART). IR-ART integrates three key phases into the iterative process, continuously removing unstable clusters and fine-tuning the vigilance parameter.
% Our experimental results demonstrate that IR-ART consistently outperforms traditional Fuzzy ART on various datasets, even under suboptimal values of \(\rho\). 这表明IR-ART对警戒参数表现出较强的鲁棒性，can be effectively applied in scenarios where clustering needs to be performed with limited expertise。同时，它没有增加预设参数的数量，保持了模糊 ART 算法的简便性和高效性，使其更容易被非专业用户使用。
% 然而，在实验过程中，我们观察到 IR-ART 可能会出现一些局限性，例如陷入重复循环、警戒区域 VR 的过度扩张，以及在处理特殊聚类形状时的挑战。因此，IR-ART 的各个方面都有很大的改进空间，如 VRE 阶段的控制策略和迭代的终止标准。此外，该方法可以作为一个通用框架，未来研究中可以与其他基于 ART 的聚类算法进行整合，为后续探索提供更多可能性。
Our experimental results show that IR-ART consistently outperforms traditional Fuzzy ART on various datasets, even with suboptimal $\rho$. This indicates that IR-ART exhibits strong robustness to \(\rho\) and can be effectively applied in scenarios where clustering needs to be performed with limited expertise. Additionally, It retains the simplicity of Fuzzy ART without adding preset parameters, making it more practical for users with limited expertise.

However, our experiments revealed some limitations of IR-ART, such as repetitive loops, excessive vigilance region expansion, and difficulties with certain cluster shapes. These issues highlight opportunities for improvement. Moreover, IR-ART can serve as a general framework that may be integrated with other ART-based clustering algorithms, offering promising directions for future research. In particular, its adaptability suggests strong potential for further application in domains such as federated learning \cite{wang2023dafkd,wang2024feddse,FedSSA,yi2024federated,liu2023cross,qi2023cross} and recommendation algorithms \cite{ma2024multimodal,ma2024plug,ma2024seedrec}.



