% \noindent \dotpara{\textbf{Offline sparse mask generation cost:}} The static sparse masks needs to be generated for each model. Although the static approach allows for sophisticated sparse mask determination methods, we find that a simple static block sum threshold is sufficient. It could also be tuned to control dense rate. Thanks to the strong generalization across prompts, we only need 1-2 prompts to determine the permutation order and then generate the sparse masks, which requires just 1-2 model inference runs (minute-level). Therefore, the cost remains manageable for practical use.

% \noindent\textbf{Hardware Implementation} We implement efficient CUDA kernels and take careful optimizations to minimize the overhead introduced by online permutation. The primary cost of the permutation lies in data movement. However, the cost can be significantly reduced by fusing permutation with previous modules. After fusing, it does not require explicitly data movement from the global memory on GPUs. Instead, we only need to modify the data address when writing back results, this incurs overhead less than 1\% of attention computation and thus negligible.

