\subsubsection{Synchronous Time and Agreement Updates}

To preserve \Cref{prop:agents_agree_on_current_agreements}, the runtime system specialises the handling of changes to \textit{asynchronous} and \textit{synchronous} control meta data.
Two kinds of changes to synchronous meta data are possible: 
\begin{enumerate*}
    \item the current time is changed to the given time, and
    \item the given agreement is added.
\end{enumerate*}
These changes have wide-reaching consequences for which actions are permissible.
Hence, they are carefully regulated, and are intended to be used sparingly.
For the sake of the experiments, we simply vest the power to make synchronous changes in a particular agent.
We call this agent \textit{consortium}, to reflect its role in expressing the consensus of all agents.


