\subsubsection{Scripted Agent Behaviour}
\label{sec:agent_scripting}
Each agent interfaces with the control plane via a dedicated, bidirectional communication channel:
agents send requests to state messages and take actions, and agents receive asynchronous gossip from their peers, and can read the synchronised control data, for example, to check the current time.


