\section{Limitations and Future Work}
\label{sec:limitation}
It is challenging to utilize our approach to conduct training when the number of candidate documents is very large. Even though this is not a significant issue during testing, since the augmentation of documents can be precomputed rather than generated online, the key techniques introduced in our approach are indeed for reducing the computational cost of generating significantly increased rollouts during training. This makes our approach more suitable for semantically complicated domains without large document sets, where retrieval performance can be boosted meanwhile computation cost remains no issue. We believe that this leads to important and meaningful future work in applying our approach to challenging IR applications. Furthermore, we believe that the bidirectional RL approach can also be of independent interest for other 
 RL scenarios where tackling the high-variance reward signals is among the key technical challenges.

