The \textnormal{pglib\_opf\_case9241\_pegase} dataset provides a highly detailed representation of the European high voltage transmission network. It includes 9,241 buses, 1,445 generators, and 16,049 branches operating across multiple voltage levels, including 750, 400, 380, 330, 220, 154, 150, 120, and 110 kV. Although the dataset is fictitious and does not reflect real-world data, it is valuable for validating optimization algorithms and simulation tools in large-scale power system research. The data were released as part of the Pan European Grid Advanced Simulation and State Estimation (PEGASE) project \cite{fliscounakis2013contingency}. 

\begin{sloppypar}
The \textnormal{pglib\_opf\_case9241\_pegase} benchmark represents one of the largest systems in the MATPOWER repository and was successfully partitioned using our graph-based spectral clustering methodology. The partitioning process ensured complete inclusion of all 9241 buses and confirmed the full connectivity of the underlying power grid graph. The best clustering configuration was determined within 10 iterations, resulting in 18 regions connected by 197 inter-regional tie-lines. The system's reference bus, numbered 4231, was assigned to Region 17 (\textnormal{mpc\_regionR17}). The reorganization of the data preserves the integrity of the original MATPOWER structure, with a total of 16049 branches and 1445 generators fully accounted for across the distributed regions. The partitioned results were saved in both \textnormal{.mat} and \textnormal{.m} formats under the name \textnormal{pglib\_opf\_case9241\_pegase\_18regions}. A visual representation of the multi-region topology is provided in Fig.~\ref{fig:case9241_partition}. This dataset has been validated by executing the distributed DC OPF and AC OPF solvers, with the convergence of the worst primal residuals depicted in Fig.~\ref{fig:case9241_residuals} with \(\rho=8000\).
\end{sloppypar}
