\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

This work presented DPLib, a reproducible and open-source benchmark library tailored for distributed and decentralized power system studies. DPLib addresses the gap in standardized datasets for distributed OPF research by offering a graph-based partitioning toolkit and over 20 multi-region test cases derived from MATPOWER. The library is complemented by modular ADMM-based DC and AC OPF solvers, which enable scalable validation across diverse case sizes. Numerical results demonstrate the accuracy of the generated test cases and convergence of the solvers, making DPLib a practical foundation for future research in scalable, privacy-preserving, and resilient power system analysis.



