Let $\infw{x}$ be a fixed point of a primitive substitution $\tau$.
If $\tau_2$ is ultimately Pisot, then the $k$-abelian complexity $(\abk{k}{x}(n))_{n\ge 0}$ is bounded for each $k\ge 1$.
