\begin{question}
 Let $\infw{x}$ be a fixed point of a substitution $\tau$.
 Consider a substitution $\sigma \colon A \to A^*$ that might be erasing and let $\infw{y} = \sigma (\infw{x})$.
 If $\tau$ is Pisot, then both $\infw{x}$ and $\infw{y}$ have automatic abelian complexities.
 Can we generalize this result to all $k$-abelian complexities? How do we compute the length-$k$ sliding-block code of the composition $\sigma \circ \tau$?
\end{question}


