    \item Let \(\text{\texttt{lb}}\) and \(\text{\texttt{ub}}\) denote the lower bound and upper bound, respectively, of the feasible region of the optimization problem \eqref{eq:global opt prob} along each dimension. 
    % \(\text{\texttt{proObj}}\) computed in Step \ref{it:proObj} is computed such that \(\text{\texttt{proObj}}\) is bounded below and above by \(\text{\ttt{lb}}\) and \(\text{\ttt{ub}}\).

